    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1082">

                <pb facs="0916" n="800" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg800"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/270.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-23T14:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 23, 1912—2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Press reports that the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Maryland</hi> is now on
                    the way to Los Mochis are giving Minister Foreign Affairs much concern. He says
                    Mexican Government has no objection to Americans there being taken away by the
                    United States, but on account of effect upon public opinion earnestly hopes that
                    vessel may be revenue cutter or transport.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
